WEBVTT

00:06.570 --> 00:08.060
Ibuki!

00:10.870 --> 00:12.670
Why didn't you call me earlier?

00:12.670 --> 00:14.040
Wait, Eykha!

00:14.040 --> 00:15.940
That's Gakusho!

00:19.050 --> 00:20.220
Eykha!

00:20.220 --> 00:21.880
Val, again!

00:29.360 --> 00:31.920
Is she really dead?

00:43.770 --> 00:47.880
Are you certain this was Gakusho's unit?

00:47.880 --> 00:50.110
It seems they were headed to Ogani Volcano.

00:50.110 --> 00:51.980
What happened...?

00:51.980 --> 00:53.550
Subleader!

00:53.550 --> 00:55.220
We found one of the villagers.

00:55.220 --> 00:58.750
A Returned One... did all this...

00:58.750 --> 01:04.660
Many villagers escaped to our fort saying that they were attacked by Returned Ones.

01:04.660 --> 01:06.930
That's why we came to investigate.

01:06.930 --> 01:11.070
Please tell me... Did the Returned Ones really appear in your village?

01:11.070 --> 01:12.470
It's not only our village...

01:12.470 --> 01:16.470
--What?
--Kouran's general was killed...

01:16.470 --> 01:18.240
She took a hit to the neck...

01:18.240 --> 01:19.470
General...?

01:19.470 --> 01:22.580
Could it be...? Lady Gakusho?

01:22.580 --> 01:24.450
Then she revived...

01:24.450 --> 01:26.180
As a Returned One?

01:26.180 --> 01:31.690
The general killed everyone, and then they all revived too!

01:31.690 --> 01:33.520
It's exactly like what happened in my village!

01:33.520 --> 01:35.490
I've never heard of any instance

01:35.490 --> 01:38.760
where those killed by a
Returned One became Returned Ones.

01:38.760 --> 01:43.930
So, where could Lady Gakusho and her unit of Returned Ones be?

01:45.170 --> 01:47.470
The name of our country is Nil Kamui.

01:47.470 --> 01:49.840
It's a small island country.

01:49.840 --> 01:54.280
The covetous, great ancient country of Kouran conducted a sudden invasion

01:54.280 --> 01:57.350
and plundered a third of the land.

01:57.350 --> 02:00.320
Our ally, the great country to the east, D'natia,

02:00.320 --> 02:04.390
defended settlements where they had their bases, then kept silent.

02:04.390 --> 02:07.360
The two great countries quickly carved away Nil Kamui's lands

02:07.360 --> 02:11.360
like meat from a sacrificial swine.

02:11.360 --> 02:14.160
The guardian deity,
Red Dragon, attacked the people,

02:14.160 --> 02:18.630
and the Returned Ones of legend began to appear.

02:18.630 --> 02:21.370
Imperial Era 3015, September...

02:21.370 --> 02:25.310
Our country was no longer ours.

02:26.310 --> 02:31.080
<i>The heat-haze shimmers, ember-toned</i>

02:31.080 --> 02:35.520
<i>Its blurred afterimage far away</i>

02:35.520 --> 02:37.650
<i>(I'm back in this life)</i>

02:48.430 --> 02:57.770
<i>My shout added to the noise</i> <i>and disappeared into the chaos</i>

02:57.770 --> 02:58.770
<i>(Don't wait)</i>

02:58.770 --> 03:00.880
<i>One single life I choose to end</i>

03:00.880 --> 03:03.950
<i>In every breath I take it ends</i>

03:03.950 --> 03:06.180
<i>One single life I choose to end</i>

03:06.180 --> 03:08.380
<i>In every breath I take it ends</i>

03:08.380 --> 03:12.620
<i>Defiling even this chosen fate</i>

03:12.620 --> 03:18.860
<i>With the blood of judgment</i>

03:18.860 --> 03:24.370
<i>"If I can just solve this unraveling</i> <i>moment with my own hands"</i>

03:24.370 --> 03:29.440
<i>I howled enough to burn my life out</i>

03:29.440 --> 03:35.110
<i>I left my hopes to an</i> <i>undependable past and vanished</i>

03:35.110 --> 03:40.720
<i>Cruelly enough, my voice was beautiful</i>

03:40.720 --> 03:44.750
<i>The ending world</i>

03:44.750 --> 03:49.620
<i>I'll be a judgment light</i>

04:04.440 --> 04:05.930
You all right?!

04:09.980 --> 04:12.480
Is that the Kouran general?

04:12.480 --> 04:14.010
What happened?!

04:24.030 --> 04:26.150
Are you okay, Ibuki?

04:54.360 --> 05:00.160
Hm, even if they are undead, destroying their brain seems to stop them.

05:00.160 --> 05:01.960
Pretty good, aren't you?

05:24.590 --> 05:28.040
Everyone, I recommend we retreat for now.

05:30.390 --> 05:32.260
--Gakusho!
--Ibuki!

05:34.060 --> 05:41.000
Ibuki, it seems you took a liking to Gakusho, despite getting to know her only recently.

05:41.000 --> 05:45.670
She... taught me the true meaning of resolve!

05:45.670 --> 05:47.240
But look at her.

05:47.240 --> 05:50.180
She's a Returned One now.

05:50.180 --> 05:57.050
There are no instances within legend of any
Returned Ones regaining their former selves.

05:57.050 --> 06:03.190
That means that the only thing we can do for her now is to make her rest in peace.

06:03.190 --> 06:05.750
Don't worry, I'll do it.

06:08.700 --> 06:12.790
We can't just defeat her and leave it at that!

06:24.580 --> 06:28.480
I do recall this flavor...

06:28.480 --> 06:30.990
It's similar to that of a dragon.

06:30.990 --> 06:34.260
So, the Returned Ones and Red Dragon...

06:34.260 --> 06:36.960
...are probably connected.

06:36.960 --> 06:38.760
Don't worry, Lou.

06:38.760 --> 06:42.230
Returned Ones wounded by me will never revive.

06:42.230 --> 06:46.670
After all, whatever residual souls remain of them are contained within me.

06:46.670 --> 06:48.800
Yes, my lord...

06:48.800 --> 06:53.140
That wound on her neck proves that Gakusho was killed by someone.

06:53.140 --> 06:55.940
Killed...? But why?

06:55.940 --> 07:01.110
Not "why," but "Who was able to kill someone so skilled as Gakusho?"

07:03.520 --> 07:05.110
Red Dragon...

07:06.650 --> 07:08.150
Answer me...!

07:10.960 --> 07:14.260
Gakusho was someone precious to me...

07:14.260 --> 07:16.630
Someone who could have become my friend.

07:16.630 --> 07:20.130
Thus, she can be taken as an offering.

07:20.130 --> 07:21.440
Indeed.

07:21.440 --> 07:24.270
Do you seek power, Imperial?

07:24.270 --> 07:29.310
I want to use your dragon flame to incinerate the person who killed Gakusho!

07:29.310 --> 07:35.120
Are you going to kill Gakusho again to kill the person who killed her?!

07:35.120 --> 07:37.990
This is the only thing I can do now...!

07:37.990 --> 07:43.120
Oh...? Quite an interesting idea he came up with.

07:43.120 --> 07:46.990
Is the dragon's power that versatile?

07:46.990 --> 07:50.330
The Returned Ones are connected to Red Dragon.

07:50.330 --> 07:57.870
In that case, I wager that Red Dragon knows that you were the one who killed Gakusho.

07:57.870 --> 08:02.140
I don't mind taking on that wager,

08:02.140 --> 08:07.550
but I would lose the means to please my lord if I were incinerated.

08:10.320 --> 08:14.890
My flames will reach any, no matter where they are.

08:14.890 --> 08:18.090
Understood. Accept the equivalence!

08:20.500 --> 08:24.570
At this distance, I can kill him using my Bai Bu Quan.

08:24.570 --> 08:28.070
There's no telling what could happen, after all...

08:28.070 --> 08:31.160
How unfortunate, Child of Contract...

08:33.910 --> 08:35.510
Lady Ulrika.

08:35.510 --> 08:37.080
Report on the expedition.

08:37.080 --> 08:40.520
It seems as if one of them, the Kouran female...

08:40.520 --> 08:43.450
...is targeting the expedition members, in an attempt to kill...

08:43.450 --> 08:46.390
Members...?!
What is going on?! Answer me!

08:49.390 --> 08:53.350
Looks like you were too focused to sense his presence.

09:22.320 --> 09:25.930
I am sorry to have arrived so late, my lord.

09:25.930 --> 09:28.960
Hien...?

09:28.960 --> 09:31.430
Yes, it is I, Hien.

09:31.430 --> 09:36.270
Agito has ordered me to guard you again.

09:36.270 --> 09:37.670
Gakusho...

09:37.670 --> 09:42.740
How dare she try to take our Child of
Contract's life using the truce as a cover?

09:46.280 --> 09:47.280
You idiot!

09:47.280 --> 09:50.690
Wh-What are you saying?

09:50.690 --> 09:52.820
Gakusho...

09:52.820 --> 09:54.760
Gakusho was...

09:54.760 --> 09:56.290
...a friend.

09:56.290 --> 09:58.630
Nonsense!

09:58.630 --> 10:00.930
Please stand up, Lord Ibuki.

10:00.930 --> 10:03.660
Our citizens would misunderstand if they saw you kneeling with your head down

10:03.660 --> 10:05.930
over the corpse of one from Kouran.

10:05.930 --> 10:09.640
Hien, you can't be friends with Ibuki.

10:09.640 --> 10:11.340
Friends?

10:11.340 --> 10:14.670
I'm merely a loyal subject of the Child of Contract.

10:17.880 --> 10:21.650
"Returned One \ Legendary beasts of mythology

10:17.880 --> 10:21.650
that were said to have laid waste to Nil Kamui.

10:17.880 --> 10:21.650
According to legend, those who held dense

10:17.880 --> 10:21.650
levels of energy within, or those who

10:17.880 --> 10:21.650
had the makings of heroes, would return

10:17.880 --> 10:21.650
from the dead in the form of a beast."

10:23.120 --> 10:25.990
"D'natia territory \ Fort Rosweisse"

10:26.720 --> 10:29.790
Excuse me for calling you all here.

10:29.790 --> 10:34.660
Sorry, but the fort houses a lot of military secrets,

10:34.660 --> 10:38.700
so we can't let the revolutionary army or Kouran see its insides.

10:38.700 --> 10:40.330
Why, of course.

10:42.800 --> 10:44.840
Lady Lou Chun Wah?

10:44.840 --> 10:45.840
Yes?

10:45.840 --> 10:48.580
By any chance, did you meet one of my subordinates?

10:48.580 --> 10:51.410
One of them is currently missing.

10:51.410 --> 10:54.880
I heard there is an item used in
D'natia that allows communication

10:54.880 --> 10:58.920
with someone from afar, similar to
Kouran's communication seal...

10:58.920 --> 11:00.860
He didn't respond...

11:00.860 --> 11:02.890
That must be quite troubling...

11:02.890 --> 11:05.220
Unfortunately, I don't know anything.

11:09.930 --> 11:13.500
Gakusho and her unit weren't the only Returned Ones?

11:13.500 --> 11:17.870
There were many villages scattered around the foot of Ogani Volcano.

11:17.870 --> 11:19.840
They were attacked by Returned Ones,

11:19.840 --> 11:22.910
and those attacked in turn became Returned Ones themselves.

11:22.910 --> 11:26.450
In the first place, where did the Returned Ones appear from?

11:26.450 --> 11:28.350
According to the villagers,

11:28.350 --> 11:32.720
the first Returned Ones to appear wore the revolutionary army's attires.

11:34.220 --> 11:36.560
Are you trying to place blame on us?

11:36.560 --> 11:38.190
Wait.

11:38.190 --> 11:41.100
Were they from the first expedition...?

11:41.100 --> 11:44.600
Yes. I heard that a unit from the revolutionary army

11:44.600 --> 11:47.070
headed to Ogani Volcano about a month ago.

11:49.570 --> 11:53.030
Everyone rose as Returned Ones...?

11:59.450 --> 12:01.780
What's this about, Ka Grava?

12:01.780 --> 12:07.050
If that's true, that means the Returned Ones are those who were killed by Red Dragon.

12:07.050 --> 12:13.590
So you think my friend's message about leaving something at Ogani Volcano is questionable?

12:13.590 --> 12:16.900
Even so, we have to go to Ogani Volcano...

12:16.900 --> 12:19.070
One moment. I must inform you

12:19.070 --> 12:23.740
that the Black Dragon Knights' third corps leader, Simeon, is headed this way.

12:23.740 --> 12:25.140
Simeon...?!

12:25.140 --> 12:26.170
Oh?

12:26.170 --> 12:28.010
So, that...

12:28.010 --> 12:30.510
Uh, who is that again?

12:30.510 --> 12:34.250
He's the leader of the Black Dragon
Knights who were sent to this island.

12:34.250 --> 12:36.350
He's third in rank among the Black Dragon Knights.

12:36.350 --> 12:39.920
Ah, and what was my rank again?

12:39.920 --> 12:42.120
Why, the lowest of them all, of course.

12:42.120 --> 12:43.820
You're ranked thirtieth.

12:45.290 --> 12:49.430
No matter what happens, our leader
Simeon can make things right.

12:49.430 --> 12:51.300
That's some faith you have in him.

12:51.300 --> 12:55.330
Yes. So please leave the rest to us.

13:00.210 --> 13:03.610
Are you still going to go to Ogani Volcano?

13:03.610 --> 13:10.320
I'm sorry, but I don't want to see any more people become like Gakusho.

13:10.320 --> 13:14.460
Well then, at least let my unit accompany you.

13:14.460 --> 13:15.820
Ulrika...

13:15.820 --> 13:20.460
I believe I was sent to protect this island's order.

13:20.460 --> 13:23.200
I can't turn my head away from the suffering of its citizens.

13:23.200 --> 13:24.690
Lord Ibuki.

13:31.910 --> 13:34.580
I know of your power, Lord Ibuki.

13:34.580 --> 13:35.640
Hien...

13:35.640 --> 13:39.180
Please kill me near Simeon!

13:39.180 --> 13:42.750
Are you telling me to incinerate
Simeon with the dragon's power?

13:42.750 --> 13:46.920
That flame will become a beacon to spread the revolution throughout the land!

13:46.920 --> 13:49.910
All in the name of ousting D'natia and Kouran!

13:51.890 --> 13:55.330
I won't kill you or Simeon.

13:55.330 --> 13:59.860
Also, Hien... You and everyone else are getting this all wrong.

14:01.370 --> 14:05.940
No matter what I do to you, nothing will happen.

14:05.940 --> 14:10.410
Lord Ibuki, you can offer the citizens of Nil Kamui to Red Dragon

14:10.410 --> 14:12.380
to gain the dragon's power.

14:12.380 --> 14:14.720
That's not it, Hien.

14:14.720 --> 14:18.690
Lord Ibuki, you are too kind.

14:18.690 --> 14:26.130
A part of me died when I lost my family-- my young sister--during the Seven Year War.

14:26.130 --> 14:29.260
No one will be saddened by my death.

14:29.260 --> 14:32.860
Having my life taken by the Child of Contract is the one and only happiness left to me.

14:34.030 --> 14:37.810
Please, use my life as you see fit!

14:37.810 --> 14:39.270
That's not the issue...!

14:39.270 --> 14:41.040
Ibuki? Hien?

14:41.040 --> 14:42.780
It looks like they're ready.

14:42.780 --> 14:44.270
Okay...

14:46.110 --> 14:48.980
Stop with your discourtesy, Kouran!

14:48.980 --> 14:50.080
Oh?

14:50.080 --> 14:53.590
In every respect, Lord Ibuki is the successor to the throne.

14:53.590 --> 14:55.660
I ask that you treat him as such!

14:55.660 --> 14:58.230
How rude of me.

14:58.230 --> 15:01.630
"Lord" Ibuki... was it?

15:02.600 --> 15:06.160
"Ogani Volcano \ Mountain path"

15:10.470 --> 15:12.610
Lord Ibuki.

15:12.610 --> 15:14.980
Did Hien tell you to call me that?

15:14.980 --> 15:16.240
Please stop.

15:16.240 --> 15:20.270
Really? How about we take the middle ground and call you "Sir Ibuki"?

15:22.980 --> 15:29.490
Meryl told me you said that if you killed
Gakusho, you could incinerate the culprit.

15:29.490 --> 15:31.760
Not me, but Red Dragon.

15:31.760 --> 15:35.600
So then in exchange for someone's life, you can gain the dragon's power to--

15:35.600 --> 15:39.330
Why don't we drop the subject already, Sir Sweallow?

15:39.330 --> 15:41.340
You knew, didn't you, Lou?

15:41.340 --> 15:43.200
Why, of course not.

15:43.200 --> 15:44.870
Such a frightening thought...

15:44.870 --> 15:46.440
I see...

15:46.440 --> 15:48.780
I think I know why you called it a curse.

15:48.780 --> 15:51.210
You mind if I ask you something?

15:51.210 --> 15:54.180
Do you really want to get rid of that power?

15:54.180 --> 15:58.020
But you're going to become
Nil Kamui's king, right?

15:58.020 --> 16:02.960
If so, that power may be something you need as king.

16:02.960 --> 16:06.290
A friend of mine died trusting in me...

16:06.290 --> 16:10.970
That's why I want to become king, so that I can put an end to sorrow.

16:10.970 --> 16:12.470
But...

16:12.470 --> 16:14.840
I don't know what I need to do...

16:14.840 --> 16:16.370
I see.

16:16.370 --> 16:20.870
In any case, I'm for the idea of getting rid of that power of yours.

16:20.870 --> 16:25.380
Why, yes... After all, that power is a major threat to D'natia.

16:25.380 --> 16:27.010
Is that how you see it?

16:32.820 --> 16:35.020
There was a village here, but...

16:35.020 --> 16:37.920
The place is just a pool of lava now.

16:42.500 --> 16:43.500
Look...!

16:43.500 --> 16:45.760
No matter how you take this...

16:47.070 --> 16:51.040
...it sure doesn't look like they're survivors waiting to be rescued.

16:51.040 --> 16:53.340
Men, forward!

16:53.340 --> 16:57.110
Hey now, what are you planning to do, Hien?

16:57.110 --> 16:59.680
We will handle the Returned Ones.

16:59.680 --> 17:00.950
Leave us be!

17:00.950 --> 17:02.720
What are you saying?!

17:02.720 --> 17:06.620
It seems like most of them were from the revolutionary army.

17:06.620 --> 17:09.360
We will deliver our friends by our own hands.

17:09.360 --> 17:10.590
Hien!

17:10.590 --> 17:13.130
Please move on ahead, Child of Contract!

17:13.130 --> 17:16.860
And please pray for their calm and eternal slumber.

17:20.800 --> 17:22.860
Rest in peace, friends!

17:32.950 --> 17:36.720
Well then, let's graciously accept his offer.

17:36.720 --> 17:40.420
After all, we are supposed to be an expedition for Red Dragon.

17:49.660 --> 17:52.270
It is Izun...

17:52.270 --> 17:54.000
Izun?

17:54.000 --> 17:56.100
Izun is in there?

17:59.340 --> 18:02.480
Now then, everyone, what should we do?

18:02.480 --> 18:04.340
We do have the option of leaving this place

18:04.340 --> 18:07.920
and letting Leader Simeon take care of the rest.

18:07.920 --> 18:09.080
Sir Sweallow...

18:09.080 --> 18:14.790
Oh, come on, we're not going to stand a chance against that huge thing!

18:14.790 --> 18:17.760
I agree with you this time.

18:17.760 --> 18:21.760
We can't take any risks that could jeopardize Ibuki or Eykha.

18:21.760 --> 18:24.470
--Right?
--I'm staying behind.

18:24.470 --> 18:25.800
Eykha...

18:25.800 --> 18:29.670
Izun would probably want me to kill him.

18:29.670 --> 18:32.370
Besides, look over there.

18:32.370 --> 18:33.710
That's...?

18:33.710 --> 18:36.310
I believe it's Red Dragon's claw.

18:36.310 --> 18:41.480
Izun fought Red Dragon by himself to save us.

18:41.480 --> 18:43.650
So that must have lodged itself there then.

18:43.650 --> 18:47.690
I see... So my friend left behind...

18:47.690 --> 18:51.160
Oh, it looks like that claw is still alive.

18:51.160 --> 18:52.860
By that, you mean...?

18:52.860 --> 18:54.630
There is way more life energy

18:54.630 --> 18:59.630
contained in Red Dragon's claw and that giant than in any normal person.

18:59.630 --> 19:02.170
This is a first for me as well.

19:02.170 --> 19:03.900
So then...?

19:03.900 --> 19:05.670
Feed me...!

19:05.670 --> 19:07.740
As you wish.

19:07.740 --> 19:09.980
Let's attack it from both sides.

19:09.980 --> 19:12.980
I can cross the lava to the other side.

19:12.980 --> 19:15.350
I will attack from behind.

19:15.350 --> 19:17.380
We'll go from the front.

19:17.380 --> 19:19.150
Before we strike...

19:19.150 --> 19:24.490
...please let me confirm whether or not Izun has really lost his sanity.

19:24.490 --> 19:25.690
Ibuki...

19:25.690 --> 19:32.400
It's possible that he still has his sanity despite becoming a Returned One.

19:32.400 --> 19:34.070
Got it.

19:34.070 --> 19:35.570
Lou...

19:35.570 --> 19:37.200
Sweallow...

19:37.200 --> 19:38.700
Please help!

19:39.740 --> 19:43.200
Well, I'll just try to stop it, then.

19:46.750 --> 19:48.450
Is stopping it your only plan?

19:48.450 --> 19:52.020
If I can move to a dead angle,
I can hide you from their sight, my lord.

19:52.020 --> 19:53.450
Ah, I see...

19:53.450 --> 19:57.080
I suppose you're serious about feeding me.

20:05.300 --> 20:07.270
Meryl, hand it over...

20:08.640 --> 20:12.770
I believe you may have forgotten, so I'll say it once more.

20:12.770 --> 20:15.400
This will disrupt the order of this island--

20:22.320 --> 20:23.880
Ahem...

20:23.880 --> 20:27.890
Well then, let us both head in from the front.

20:27.890 --> 20:29.960
No, Lady Ulrika.

20:29.960 --> 20:31.830
I'd like to ask you to take care of Meryl.

20:31.830 --> 20:34.600
Please watch us from behind.

20:34.600 --> 20:37.100
It's not that I'm underestimating a newcomer such as yourself, but...

20:37.100 --> 20:39.770
I know you're strong.

20:39.770 --> 20:42.300
That's why I'd like you to stay behind.

20:42.300 --> 20:48.110
And when we reach our limit, I'd like you to at least have those children escape.

20:50.410 --> 20:54.820
In the end, Sir Sweallow isn't attached to me.

20:54.820 --> 20:58.750
To him, what needs to be protected is the future.

20:58.750 --> 21:04.360
Are you saying you're willing to offer your life for the expedition's mission?

21:04.360 --> 21:09.660
You know, it was the first time someone asked me for help.

21:11.200 --> 21:12.830
Keep one thing in mind.

21:12.830 --> 21:15.700
Do not place trust in that nun, Lou.

21:17.170 --> 21:21.630
Don't worry. I'm used to being tricked by females.

21:23.480 --> 21:26.180
Quite a fine master you have there.

21:26.180 --> 21:29.380
He's... just a good-for-nothing.

21:46.000 --> 21:46.470
"Act 6"

21:47.400 --> 21:50.700
"Act 6 \ Six Paths of Transmigration"

21:57.640 --> 22:02.880
<i>The end I thought I'd chosen;</i> <i>though the melody may warp (more)</i>

22:02.880 --> 22:07.850
<i>At last the pounding heartbeat</i> <i>desires it and performs</i>

22:07.850 --> 22:13.090
<i>Both the evened-out impulse</i> <i>and the wiped-out lament (now)</i>

22:13.090 --> 22:19.560
<i>Are wings that race onward,</i> <i>tearing through the fog</i>

22:32.910 --> 22:42.860
<i>Emotions that can't be hidden in words</i> <i>that push people away (bleeding through)</i>

22:42.860 --> 22:48.060
<i>Emptying both hands so I can get what I want</i>

22:48.060 --> 22:55.560
<i>If I can't even find fault</i> <i>with this unshrinking expanse</i>

22:56.770 --> 22:58.310
<i>What am I supposed to believe?</i>

22:58.310 --> 23:02.480
<i>I need nothing if I have you:</i>
<i>That alone is enough</i>

23:02.480 --> 23:12.480
<i>Go on and cry: You burn so bright because</i> <i>the gears of transmigration are turning</i>

23:12.620 --> 23:22.620
<i>Tightly spin together the intertwining roads</i> <i>to which your shouts led you</i>

23:26.930 --> 23:27.000
Act 7: "Ups and Downs in Life."

23:27.000 --> 23:30.440
"Act 7: Ups and Downs in Life."

23:27.000 --> 23:27.470
"Act 7"

23:30.440 --> 23:32.970
Those with form soon break...

23:32.970 --> 23:37.280
Sweallow Clazzvali is a swordsman who is an embodiment of that rule.

23:37.280 --> 23:40.910
Is it a sin for a person to dream of eternity?
